Enumerate installed fonts on iOS via native bridge

On iOS/iPadOS, WKWebView does not support the Browser Font Access API
(queryLocalFonts), so getFontSnippets() returns [] — leaving the
editor.fontFamily and terminal.integrated.fontFamily settings without
autocomplete.

When the iOS wrapper bridge is available, call listFonts() to query
UIFont.familyNames (which includes both system and user-installed fonts
on iOS). The returned families are formatted as IJSONSchemaSnippets for
the settings autocomplete.

Note: actual font rendering works automatically — WKWebView sees all
installed system fonts via CSS `font-family`, no @font-face needed.
This patch only enables the setting autocomplete.

